---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { personSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="About Balbina Garza Delgado | Child & Adolescent Psychotherapist, Bath"
  description="Balbina Garza Delgado is an accredited child and adolescent psychotherapist in Bath, with more than 20 years of experience in private practice, CAMHS, schools and fostering."
  jsonLd={[personSchema()]}
>
  <div class="page-head page-head-portrait">
    <div class="container portrait-grid">
      <div class="portrait-text">
        <h1>Balbina Garza Delgado</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Child and adolescent psychotherapist, working in Bath and online.<br />
          BSc, MA, MSc, MACP.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="portrait"
        src="/portrait.webp"
        width="840"
        height="917"
        alt="Pencil portrait of Balbina Garza Delgado, smiling, with long dark hair"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        I have worked with children and families for more than 20 years. In that time I have seen how
        difficult behaviour and painful emotions touch a whole family, and why early understanding and
        support matter so much.
      </p>
      <p>
        Emotional wellbeing underpins learning, growth and relationships. Difficulties in infancy or
        early childhood, such as trauma, domestic violence, struggles with attachment or overwhelming
        feelings, can shape a child's later schooling, relationships and confidence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Research from the Anna Freud Centre (Allison and Campbell, 2019) suggests that half of mental
        health problems are established by the age of 14, and three quarters by 24. That is a strong
        reason to offer help early.
      </p>
      <p>
        Psychotherapy can help parents understand what a child is communicating through a symptom or a
        behaviour. My commitment is to prevention, and to helping children understand their own minds and
        feelings so they can build resilient lives.
      </p>

      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <p>
        My work spans private practice, CAMHS in the NHS, schools and fostering agencies. I have worked
        with children, adolescents, young adults and parents, and with young people in care and their
        carers. Where it helps the child, I work alongside social workers, schools and other health
        professionals. I offer therapy, parent work, consultations and supervision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <h2>Education and training</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="timeline">
        <li><span class="when">2008 to 2012</span><span>Four-year full-time training in Child and Adolescent Psychotherapy, British Psychotherapy Foundation</span></li>
        <li><span class="when">2007 to 2008</span><span>MSc Psychoanalytic Developmental Psychology, Anna Freud Centre/University College London</span></li>
        <li><span class="when">2000 to 2002</span><span>MA Clinical Psychology and Adult Psychotherapy, Universidad Anáhuac, Mexico City</span></li>
        <li><span class="when">1994 to 1998</span><span>BSc Psychology, Northeastern University, Boston, USA</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <h2>Registration</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li>Qualified Child and Adolescent Psychotherapist</li>
          <li>Accredited member of the Association of Child Psychotherapists (ACP), which is recognised by the Professional Standards Authority</li>
          <li>Qualified adult psychologist in Mexico</li>
          <li>Up-to-date enhanced DBS check</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta />
</Base>
